<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To determine the time it takes to administer the loading dose, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the mass of the child to kilograms**:  
   \( 32 \text{ lb} \times 2.205 \text{ kg/lb} = 70.96 \text{ kg} \).

2. **Calculate the loading dose**:  
   \( 70.96 \text{ kg} \times 20 \text{ mg/kg} = 1419.2 \text{ mg} \).

3. **Calculate the time required**:  
   \( \frac{1419.2 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 2838.4 \text{ min} \).

The total time to administer the dose is \(\boxed{2838.4 \text{ minutes}}\).
