C3H8 + 5O2 → 3CO2 + 4H2O

Given the standard enthalpy of combustion of propane (C3H8) is -2220 kJ/mol.

Since the enthalpy of combustion is given per mole of propane, we can multiply the number of moles of propane (2.5 moles) by the enthalpy of combustion to find the total heat released:

Heat released = moles of propane × enthalpy of combustion
Heat released = 2.5 moles × (-2220 kJ/mol)
Heat released = -5550 kJ

