","The entropy change (ΔS) for the reaction is calculated as follows:

\[
\Delta S = \sum \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \sum \Delta S_{\text{reactants}} = \left( \Delta S_{\text{PbO}} + \Delta S_{\text{SO}_2} \right) - \left( 2 \Delta S_{\text{PbS}} + 3 \Delta S_{\text{O}_2} \right)
\]

Substituting the given entropies:

\[
\Delta S = \left( 2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2 \right) - \left( 2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1 \right)
\]

\[
\Delta S = (133 + 496.4) - (182.4 + 615.3)
\]

\[
\Delta S = 629.4 - 797.7
\]

\[
\Delta S = -168.3 \text{ J/K mol}
\]

