","To calculate the power output of the galvanic cell, we first need to determine the cell potential (E) using the Nernst equation. The cell potential is then used to calculate the current (I) and finally, the power output (P).

1. **Cell Potential (E):**
   The cell consists of a hydrogen electrode (anode) and a copper electrode (cathode). The reaction is:
   \[
   \text{Zn(s)} + \text{Cu}^{2+}(aq) \rightarrow \text{Zn}^{2+}(aq) + \text{Cu(s)}
   \]

