\]
(c) To evaluate the integral $\int_{0}^{1} 2^{2 y} d y$, we use the substitution $u = 2y$, so $du = 2 dy$, and $du/2 = dy$. The integral becomes:
\[
\int_{0}^{1} 2^{2 y} d y = \frac{1}{2} \int_{0}^{2} 2^u du = \frac{1}{2} \left[ \frac{1}{\ln 2} 2^u \right]_{0}^{2} = \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{1}{\ln 2} 2^2 - \frac{1}{\ln 2} 2^0 \right) = \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{4}{\ln 2} - \frac{1}{\ln 2} \right) = \frac{3}{2 \ln 2}.
