\]
For a vector field \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\), the components are \(\mathbf{V} = \mathbf{V}_1(x, y) = \langle \mathbf{V}_1(x, y), \mathbf{V}_2(x, y), \mathbf{V}_3(x, y) \rangle\). Since \(\mathbf{V}\) depends only on \(x\) and \(y\), it can be written as:
\[
\mathbf{V}(x, y) = \langle \mathbf{V}_1(x, y), \mathbf{V}_2(x, y), \mathbf{V}_3(x, y) \).
\]
The curl of \(\mathbf{V}\) is given by:
\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_3}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_2}{\partial y} + \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_2}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \mathbf{V}_3}{\partial y}.
\]
