The energy resolution \(Q\) is related to the natural width \(\Gamma\) of the particle by the formula:

\[
Q \geq \hbar \Gamma
\]

Given the lifetime \(T \approx 2.0 \times 10^{-23}\text{ s}\), the natural width is:

\[
\Gamma = \frac{1}{2T} = \frac{1}{2 \times 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}} = 2.5 \times 10^{22} \text{ s}^{-1}
\]

The energy resolution \(Q\) is:

\[
