\[
Q \approx 6.7 \times 10^{-13} \text{ J} \times \frac{1 \text{ MeV}}{1.602 \times 10^{-13} \text{ J}} \approx 4.2 \text{ MeV}
\]

The total resolution \(Q_{\text{total}}\) is typically the sum of the intrinsic resolution and the radiative correction. The radiative correction is typically 1.2 times the natural width, so:

\[
Q_{\text{total}} \approx 4.2 \text{ MeV}
\]

The range of outcomes for the measurement of the Σ⁺ rest energy is:

\[
\Delta E \approx \pm Q_{\text{total}} = \pm 4.2 \text{ MeV}
\]

Thus, the expected range of outcomes for measurements of the Σ⁺ rest energy is:

\[
\boxed{1385 \pm 4.2 \text{ MeV}}
