","To determine the entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) for the rubbing of two bodies, we use the concept of entropy production in friction. The entropy production rate is given by:

\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]

where:
- \( F_{\text{fr}} \) is the friction force,
- \( v \) is the mean relative velocity of the bodies,
- \( T \) is the room temperature.

This formula arises from the fact that friction converts mechanical energy into heat, which increases the entropy of the system. The entropy production rate is the rate at which entropy is generated due to this process.

Thus, the entropy production rate is:

\[
\boxed{\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}
\]",relevance,"# Task Description
