</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The index of refraction (n) of a medium for light is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum (c) to the speed of light in the medium (v):

n = c / v

In this case, the speed of light in the plastic (v) is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum (c). So, v = 0.680c.

Now, we can plug this value into the formula for the index of refraction:

n = c / (0.680c)

The speed of light (c) cancels out:

n = 1 / 0.680

n ≈ 1.46

So, the index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic is approximately 1.46.
