","(a) The magnitude of the acceleration of the proton is calculated using Newton's second law:  
\[ F = m a \]  
The force on the proton is given by the electric field:  
\[ F = q E \]  
Substituting \( F = q E \) into Newton's second law:  
\[ q E = m a \]  
Solving for acceleration:  
\[ a = \frac{q E}{m} = \frac{(1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C})}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.8 \times 10^{11} \, \text{m/s}^2 \]  

(b) The proton starts from rest, so its initial speed is \( v_0 = 0 \, \text{m/s} \). The proton accelerates to a final speed of \( v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s} \). Using the kinematic equation:  
\[ v = v_0 + a t \]  
Solving for time:  
\[ t = \frac{v - v_0}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s} - 0}{4.8 \times 10^{11} \, \text{m/s}^2} = 7.25 \times 10^{-8} \, \text{s} \]  

