","The decay length of an evanescent wave is given by:
\[
\delta = \frac{\lambda}{2\pi (n_f - n_e)}
\]
where:
- \(\lambda\) is the wavelength,
- \(n_f\) is the refractive index of the free medium (e.g., air),
- \(n_e\) is the effective refractive index of the waveguide.

Given:
- \(\lambda = 1 \, \mu\text{m} = 10^{-6} \, \text{m}\)
- \(n_f - n_e \approx 0.3\)

Substituting these values:
\[
\delta = \frac{10^{-6}}{2\pi (0.3)} = \frac{10^{-6}}{0.6\pi} \approx 5.3 \times 10^{-7} \, \text{m} = 530 \, \mu\text{m}
\]

