   The horizontal velocity \( v'_x = v_x = v \cos \theta \).  
   The final velocity \( v' \) has components \( v'_x = v \cos \theta \) and \( v'_y = -\frac{1}{3} v \sin \theta \).  
   The fraction of the horizontal velocity is \( \frac{v'_x}{v} = \cos \theta \), and the fraction of the vertical velocity is \( \frac{v'_y}{v} = -\frac{1}{3} \sin \theta \).

