","The Higgs boson, discovered in 2012 at the Large Hadron Collider (LHC), is a fundamental particle in the Standard Model of particle physics. It is responsible for giving mass to other particles through the Higgs mechanism. By studying the various decay modes of the Higgs boson, physicists can test the predictions of the Standard Model and search for new physics beyond it.

